codex
The proof has no proof-local operational bridge or oracle: `verification.k` adds only three exact program macros and five terminating mathematical functions. The only result-bearing abstraction on the reachable path is the supplied semantics’ opaque `sortVS`; I’m treating it as an explicit external trust boundary and separating its finite integer-list evidence from what K proves symbolically. I’m now generating the exhaustive declaration/rule inventory and a construct-to-rule map.
apply patch
